{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRK7gx16Sj6uFGrXo3Yv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fxv9pH8ak1jrokpd3LpyBk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-4xNgoj/memory/invoice-currency-follows-region.md","content":"---\nname: invoice-currency-follows-region\ndescription: Decision: invoice currency is derived from the customer's region (EU=EUR, UK=GBP, any US_* region=USD), never from the request\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nAn invoice's currency always follows the customer's region:\n- EU -> EUR\n- UK -> GBP\n- every US region (US_CA, US_NY, and any other US_*) -> USD\n\nThe currency is never taken from the request payload.\n\n**Why:** A client once sent USD for a German customer and the bank rejected the payout.\n\n**How to apply:** When writing or reviewing invoice code, derive currency from the customer's region via a region-to-currency mapping. Ignore or reject any currency field supplied by the client. Treat all US_* regions as USD, not just the ones currently listed. No code change was requested at the time of this decision (2026-11-26).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_read_input_tokens":22032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":552,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"432e436e-af3e-4e18-b812-617793c2af90","uuid":"4e618f8c-7e59-4de7-8877-af1e82ead5e2","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:36:12.530Z","request_id":"req_011ChRK7gopALFnKXAJQHVQd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Fxv9pH8ak1jrokpd3LpyBk":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-4xNgoj/memory/invoice-currency-follows-region.md","content":"---\nname: invoice-currency-follows-region\ndescription: Decision: invoice currency is derived from the customer's region (EU=EUR, UK=GBP, any US_* region=USD), never from the request\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nAn invoice's currency always follows the customer's region:\n- EU -> EUR\n- UK -> GBP\n- every US region (US_CA, US_NY, and any other US_*) -> USD\n\nThe currency is never taken from the request payload.\n\n**Why:** A client once sent USD for a German customer and the bank rejected the payout.\n\n**How to apply:** When writing or reviewing invoice code, derive currency from the customer's region via a region-to-currency mapping. Ignore or reject any currency field supplied by the client. Treat all US_* regions as USD, not just the ones currently listed. No code change was requested at the time of this decision (2026-11-26).\n"}}}
